Z||000000||Alex4mula||07-05-2001||02:19 PM||||I was testing an auto 88 Formula and it ran at 2500 RPM at 55MPH and 3000 RPM at 70 MPH. Is that ok? I found it a little bit high compared to my 5 speed but I know final drive ratio may be different. TIA.||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBert||07-05-2001||02:21 PM||||That's real close to my 86GT.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||07-05-2001||04:04 PM||||That sounds about right.  The first time I test drove a V6 auto I thought the torque converter wasn't locking up.  The RPM's seemed way to high compared to the V6 5sp and 4 cyl auto's I had driven.  As I understand it the V6 auto has a higher final drive ratio for better performance while the 4 cyl auto's are geared more for economy.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
